  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with scvi_n200 (config_002) achieves 0.520 acc, while image-only with ViT-L (config_041) is very weak at 0.227 acc. We have no multimodal results yet, so the central uncertainty is whether adding the image modality to the strong RNA signal provides complementary information or merely adds noise. Question: config_005 (multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, concat fusion, no aggregation) is the simplest possible multimodal combination using the best-performing RNA encoder. It isolates the core question—does any fusion of image into RNA help—without confounding from multiprofile, aggregation, or more complex fusion. Why this is the best next experiment: if concat fusion fails to beat 0.520, we gain strong evidence that the image modality (as currently encoded) is not informative and can deprioritize the large multimodal configuration space, saving budget. If it does beat 0.520, we confirm a promising direction and can then systematically explore fusion type, aggregation, and multiprofile. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the highest-level design decision (multimodal vs. unimodal) before committing to more complex variants."
}

